{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK10OidcPolicyV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcPolicy","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","title":"OidcPolicy"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:sensitiveScopesEnabled:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(from:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedScopes","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrMaxClients","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/defaultLocale","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dynamicRegistration","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/externalClientAllowedResources","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is which is the whole of what ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_tenant_override"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clamp_overrides_to_org"},{"type":"text","text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mfa_enforced"},{"type":"text","text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dynamic_registration"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the ladder "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"type":"text","text":" → "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initial_access_token"},{"type":"text","text":" →"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":": a tenant may move down it and never up. * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_max_clients"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days"},{"type":"text","text":"], on the ordinary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tenant <= org"},{"type":"text","text":" rule — with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wrinkle that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" on the second means "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"never sweep","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", which is the longest window of all and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is handled by ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_ttl_strictness"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", therefore never validated against the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"baseline and never clamped: * ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::default_locale"},{"type":"text","text":"]. A language is a presentation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preference; there is no sense in which Italian is stricter than French. *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes"},{"type":"text","text":"], ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts"},{"type":"text","text":"] and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"]. Each names per-tenant resources — "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant’s MCP servers, "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" tenant’s callback hosts — and there is no sense in which one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would force an organization to enumerate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline before any tenant could name one. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more restrictive”, which binds every field that "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a restrictiveness; a field that has none cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both groups and is checked on the resolved policy rather than on either input: see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate_dcr_policy"},{"type":"text","text":"]."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OidcPolicy"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrAllowedScopes":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedScopes","type":"topic","title":"dcrAllowedScopes","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrallowedscopes","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedScopes","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — the scopes a self-registered client may ask for. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scope"},{"type":"text","text":" a registration names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is not on this list is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_client_metadata"},{"type":"text","text":"; an empty list means a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-registered client gets no scopes at all, which is the honest default for a tenant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that has turned registration on without deciding what it grants. May not contain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"address","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"phone","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — see this module’s [","type":"text"},{"code":"sensitive_scope_in_dcr_list","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays":{"title":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — how long an externally registered client survives without being used. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"DEFAULT_DCR_UNUSED_CLIENT_TTL_DAYS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" disables the sweep for this tenant, which an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operator who prunes out of band may legitimately want. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two sweeps read it, over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different clocks","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (T21.8). A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: dcr"},{"type":"text","text":" row is measured from its last"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization, falling back to when it was registered. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"managed_by: cimd"},{"type":"text","text":" row is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the last time its document was "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"presented","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", which every authorize, token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and PAR request moves — so a document in daily use is never swept however old its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration is, and one nobody has presented since the window is, and re-materialises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the next request if it is still published. Like the ceiling, it keeps its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dcr_"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrunusedclientttldays","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/SE":{"title":"Swift.Encodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/Se":{"title":"Swift.Decodable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/externalClientAllowedResources":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/externalclientallowedresources","title":"externalClientAllowedResources","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/externalClientAllowedResources","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"externalClientAllowedResources"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"D3"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the audiences an externally registered client may address. The single most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"important field on this policy, and the reason the settings handler refuses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration: anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":" while it is empty. A client an unrelated party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered cannot declare its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"allowed_resources"},{"type":"text","text":"; it inherits this list verbatim,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so what a stranger can mint a token "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"for"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a decision the tenant took in advance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than one the registration request makes. Empty means an externally registered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client can obtain only today’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam:user"},{"type":"text","text":" tokens — which AXIAM’s own APIs accept. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is why the interlock exists: the empty list is not a safe default for an "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration endpoint, it is the most dangerous one. Shared with T5 (CIMD), which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inherits the same list for the same reason."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dynamicRegistration":{"title":"dynamicRegistration","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — whether a client may register itself (RFC 7591), and on what terms. "},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unless somebody says otherwise (I1)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dynamicRegistration","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dynamicregistration","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dynamicRegistration","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/defaultLocale":{"title":"defaultLocale","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The BCP 47 tag the sign-in page falls back to when the relying party’s "},{"code":"ui_locales","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selects nothing (W5’s chain, plan §4.6). "},{"code":"None","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means “no tenant preference”, which"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lands on the deployment default (","type":"text"},{"code":"en","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the behaviour every deployment had before this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"field existed. A tag this build does not ship also lands there: the parse is exact","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than a language lookup, so a stored ","type":"text"},{"code":"fr-CA","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads as “somebody wrote something"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this binary does not ship” rather than as a guess at French. Stored as a string rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Locale"},{"type":"text","text":" enum because that enum lives in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam-oauth2"},{"type":"text","text":", four layers above"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this crate, and the crate layering points inward."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/defaultLocale","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/defaultlocale","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultLocale","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:sensitiveScopesEnabled:)":{"title":"init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:sensitiveScopesEnabled:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(cimd:dcrAllowedRedirectHosts:dcrAllowedScopes:dcrMaxClients:dcrUnusedClientTTLDays:defaultLocale:dynamicRegistration:externalClientAllowedResources:sensitiveScopesEnabled:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/init(cimd:dcrallowedredirecthosts:dcrallowedscopes:dcrmaxclients:dcrunusedclientttldays:defaultlocale:dynamicregistration:externalclientallowedresources:sensitivescopesenabled:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"cimd","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","text":"CimdPolicy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedScopes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrMaxClients","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultLocale","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dynamicRegistration","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"externalClientAllowedResources","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts":{"title":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrallowedredirecthosts","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — hosts a self-registered client’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"redirect_uris","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may point at, as globs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"*.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for any). The loopback hosts (","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"[::1]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are always allowed whatever this says, because RFC 8252 §7.3 is how every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"desktop MCP client receives its callback and a tenant that forbade them would have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turned registration on for nobody.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/encode(to:)":{"abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"encode(to:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/encode(to:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"encode"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Encoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrMaxClients":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrMaxClients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrmaxclients","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrMaxClients","title":"dcrMaxClients","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — how many externally registered clients this tenant may hold. See","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"DEFAULT_DCR_MAX_CLIENTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Counted once per mechanism, against the same number"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(T21.8): ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: dcr","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rows and ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: cimd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rows each have this many. So a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant running both cannot have shadow rows materialised from documents exhaust the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allowance for self-registration, or the reverse. The CIMD count is checked ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document is fetched, so a tenant at its ceiling is not an outbound amplifier either. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" name because dynamic registration defined it, on the same precedent as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(from:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/init(from:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(from:)","title":"init(from:)","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":": any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","text":"Decoder"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/cimd":{"title":"cimd","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cimd","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CimdPolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/cimd","abstract":[{"text":"T21.5 — whether a URL-shaped ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is resolved by fetching the document it names,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and on what terms. See [","type":"text"},{"code":"CimdPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]; off unless somebody turns it on (I1). Nested, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore inherited or overridden ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"whole","type":"text"}]},{"text":": the fields are terms of one decision, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"half-merged posture is one neither the organization nor the tenant wrote.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/sensitiveScopesEnabled":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/sensitivescopesenabled","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","abstract":[{"text":"Whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"address"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"phone"},{"type":"text","text":" may be registered on a client, requested at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"authorization endpoint, and released at UserInfo (X7 G8). ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Off unless an organization","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"turns it on.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" The two scopes release a postal address and a telephone number —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"categories of personal data AXIAM has no other use for — so the deployment that has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never thought about them releases nothing, and the operator who has thought about them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says so once, at the organization level, where the lawful basis for holding the data was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"decided. The switch is a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"capability","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", not a grant: with it on, a client still has to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"register the scope, the request still has to ask for it, and the user still has to have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"consented. It is the first of four gates, and it is the only one an operator can close","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for everybody at once.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenID Connect surface controls (X7 G8, plan §4.6\/§4.8; T21.4). Settings that are not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"password rules, here because this is the org-baseline-plus-tenant-override surface every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other per-tenant control lives on. They are not all of the same kind as each other, and"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which is which is the whole of what [","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_tenant_override","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"clamp_overrides_to_org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] read, so it is set out rather than inferred. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tenant may be stricter than its organization and never more permissive: *"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self::sensitive_scopes_enabled"},{"type":"text","text":"], validated "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"disable-only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — the mirror image of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"mfa_enforced","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because releasing personal data is the less-restrictive direction, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant can turn its organization’s decision off but never on. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dynamic_registration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ladder ","type":"text"},{"code":"disabled","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" → ","type":"text"},{"code":"initial_access_token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" →","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"anonymous","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": a tenant may move down it and never up. * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_max_clients","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_unused_client_ttl_days","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], on the ordinary ","type":"text"},{"code":"tenant <= org","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule — with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrinkle that ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the second means ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never sweep"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", which is the longest window of all and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is handled by [","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_ttl_strictness","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Not ordered","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", therefore never validated against the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"baseline and never clamped: * [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::default_locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. A language is a presentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preference; there is no sense in which Italian is stricter than French. *","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"], [","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_redirect_hosts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"] and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::external_client_allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. Each names per-tenant resources — ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant’s MCP servers, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"this","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" tenant’s callback hosts — and there is no sense in which one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such list is stricter than another. A subset rule would force an organization to enumerate","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every tenant’s resource servers in its own baseline before any tenant could name one. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"model’s rule is “a tenant may only be more restrictive”, which binds every field that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"has"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a restrictiveness; a field that has none cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both groups and is checked on the resolved policy rather than on either input: see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_dcr_policy","type":"codeVoic